<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111831" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλοῖσβος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>any confused roaring noise,</i>
			in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> of <i>the noise of battle,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.322
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				469
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.416
			</span></i> (never in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν μὲν ἄρ᾽ ἐκ φλοίσβου . . ῥύσαντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Euph.
					23
				</span></i>
			; of the sea, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόντου περῶσα φλοῖσβον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					792
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				479
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hymn.Is.</u>
				166
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλοίσβων δίναις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					379
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰλυόεις φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					1.777
				</span></i>
			.—Poet. word.</div>
